---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
const updated = 'June 8, 2026';
---
<LegalLayout title="Privacy Policy" updated={updated} path="/privacy" description="How Stride collects, uses, and protects your data — including location used to track your runs.">
  <p>This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>Stride</strong> ("Stride", "we", "us") collects, uses, and shares information when you use the Stride mobile app and <a href="/">striderunning.run</a> (the "Service"). By using the Service you agree to this Policy.</p>

  <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
  <h3>You give us</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account:</strong> email, username, display name, optional avatar and bio.</li>
    <li><strong>Content you create:</strong> runs, posts, comments, clubs, events, and your chosen territory colour and flag.</li>
    <li><strong>Waitlist:</strong> if you join from the website, your email address.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Collected as you run</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Precise location (GPS):</strong> we record your route <em>while you actively track a run</em> to calculate distance, pace, and the territory you enclose. You can deny location and use explore mode.</li>
    <li><strong>Activity data:</strong> distance, duration, pace, elevation, and captured area.</li>
    <li><strong>Approximate location/city:</strong> derived from your device to power city leaderboards and nearby-event notifications.</li>
    <li><strong>Device & usage:</strong> app version, device model, and diagnostics for stability and security.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. How we use information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Provide the core game — track runs, compute and display territory, and run leaderboards, leagues, clubs and events.</li>
    <li>Send you notifications you’ve enabled (e.g., your turf was taken, a nearby event, streak reminders).</li>
    <li>Maintain safety, prevent cheating and abuse, and enforce our Terms.</li>
    <li>Improve the Service and fix problems.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. How we share information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>With other players:</strong> your username, avatar, tier, territory (shape, colour, m²) and public posts are visible to others by design. Manage visibility in privacy settings.</li>
    <li><strong>Service providers</strong> who process data on our behalf: Supabase (database, authentication, storage), Mapbox (maps), Expo/Apple (push notifications), and Sentry (crash diagnostics).</li>
    <li><strong>Legal:</strong> when required by law or to protect rights and safety.</li>
    <li>We <strong>do not sell</strong> your personal information.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Your choices & rights</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Turn location off in iOS Settings (you can still explore; you can’t claim territory).</li>
    <li>Set activity privacy (everyone / followers / private) and hide from leaderboards.</li>
    <li>Access, correct, or <strong>delete your account and data</strong> in-app (Settings → Delete account), which cascades your runs and territory.</li>
    <li>Depending on where you live (e.g., EEA/UK/California), you may have additional rights to access, port, or restrict processing — contact us to exercise them.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Data retention & security</h2>
  <p>We keep data while your account is active and as needed for legal and security purposes, then delete or anonymise it. We use industry-standard safeguards (encryption in transit, row-level security, restricted access), but no method is 100% secure.</p>

  <h2>6. Children</h2>
  <p>Stride is not directed to children under 13 (or the minimum age in your country), and we do not knowingly collect their data. If you believe a child has provided us data, contact us and we will delete it.</p>

  <h2>7. International transfers</h2>
  <p>Your information may be processed in countries other than your own, including the United States. We rely on appropriate safeguards where required.</p>

  <h2>8. Changes</h2>
  <p>We’ll update this Policy as the Service evolves and revise the “Last updated” date. Material changes will be notified in-app or by email.</p>

  <h2>9. Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions or requests: <a href="mailto:privacy@striderunning.run">privacy@striderunning.run</a>.</p>
</LegalLayout>
